include ../mixins/head.pug
doctype html
html(lang="en")
  // HTML Head
  +project_head('Serendipity - Max Nielsen')
  
  body
    // Header
    include includes/header
    
    // Title and nav(?)
    picture.project-hero-img.serendipity-hero-img
      source(
        srcset="../../img/design/serendipity/design-context.webp" 
        media="(min-width: 58.125rem)"
        )
      source(
        srcset="../../img/design/serendipity/selector.webp" 
        media="(max-width: 58.125rem)"
        )
      img(src="../../img/design/serendipity/selector.webp")

    // About Me
    #main.two-col
      aside(id="table_of_contents")
        h1(id="table_of_contents_title") Serendipity
        p.tagline
          | A shared listening experience for large student design spaces of the near
          |   future.
        div(id="project_details")
          .project-details.details-border
            .h-btn
              h2.details-title(id="project_details_title") Project details
              a.button-tiny.button-small.button-toggle(
                data-hide-text="Hide" 
                data-show-text="Show" 
                id="project_details_toggle"
                href="#"
                aria-labelledby="project_details_toggle project_details"
								aria-expanded="true"
								aria-controls="project_details_wrapper") Hide
            .project-details-wrapper(id="project_details_wrapper")
              .project-for.project-detail-item
                h3 Group project for
                a.button-tiny(
                  href="https://tue.osiris-student.nl/onderwijscatalogus/extern/cursus?cursuscode=DBSU10&collegejaar=2023" 
                  target="_blank"
                  )
                  | DBSU10
                  |   - Designing Connected Experiences
              .project-detail-item
                h3 Timeframe
                p April 2024 (8 weeks)
              .project-detail-item
                h3 Project focus
                ul.smaller-list-indent
                  li Physical prototyping
                  li DIY networked electronics
                  li Interaction/system design
              .project-detail-item
                h3 Tools used
                ul.smaller-list-indent
                  li HTML/CSS/JS
                  li Music steaming service APIs
                  li Arduino electronics
              .project-detail-item
                h3 The team
                ul.smaller-list-indent
                  li
                    a.button-tiny(
                      target="_blank" 
                      href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maarten-van-der-hart-b420a5167/"
                      ) Maarten van der Hart
                  li
                    a.button-tiny(
                      target="_blank" 
                      href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stan-wijnen-1594981ab/"
                      ) Stan Wijnen
              .project-detail-item
                h3 What I did
                p
                  | I designed and created the system of how it selects music in a fair manner, Serendipity’s
                  |   web interface, and most of the Arduino code.
        #toc.toc
          h2 In this piece
          ul
            li
              a(
                data-target="what_it_is" 
                href="#what_it_is"
                ) What it is
            li
              a(
                data-target="voting_system_imbalance" 
                href="#voting_system_imbalance"
                )
                | Voting system imbalance
            li
              a(
                data-target="web_interface_features" 
                href="#web_interface_features"
                )
                | Web interface features
            li
              a(
                data-target="reflection" 
                href="#reflection"
                ) Reflection
      #article
        section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="what_it_is")
          h2.heading-underline What it is
          .explanation-wrapper
            div
              p.summary-text
                | Serendipity is a DIY physical and digital system where everyone in a large collaborative
                |   space can vote for music they want played and shared within that space. Three physical
                |   devices allow individuals to vote for a "vibe" (mood) of music. A random vibe is drawn from
                |   that voting pool, playing that type of music.
              p.summary-text
                | People can visit Serendipity's website to see what music is playing,
                |   and, if they like the song, quickly add it to their playlist.
              p.summary-text
                | As part of a three-person group, I designed and created the system of
                |   how it selects music in a fair manner, Serendipity’s web interface, and most of the Arduino
                |   code.
            .trailer.subheading
              h3.heading-underline Watch the trailer here
              iframe(
                allowfullscreen="" 
                referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" 
                allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" 
                title="YouTube video player" 
                src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/DHk9P7hJ0ig?si=3ILLlr82pMtRjBcy" 
                height="315" 
                width="560"
                )
        section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="voting_system_imbalance")
          h2.heading-underline Voting system imbalance
          .explanation-wrapper.two-sections
            div
              .subheading
                h3.heading-underline Original voting system
                img(
                  alt="Winner-takes-all system" 
                  id="before_img" 
                  width="3604" 
                  height="998" 
                  src="../../img/design/serendipity/system1.webp"
                  )
              p
                | Originally, we had a majority rules-based method of choosing vibes: the most popular vibe
                |   voted for would always be played.
              p
                | A hands-on critique session with students and instructors helped us discover an imbalance in
                |   voting power. With this majority rules system, one’s taste in less popular vibes would never
                |   be heard.
            div
              .subheading
                h3.heading-underline New voting system
                img(
                  alt="Lottery system" 
                  id="after_img" 
                  width="3604" 
                  height="998" 
                  src="../../img/design/serendipity/system2.webp"
                  )
              p
                | After that critique session, I initiated a roundtable discussion to disseminate feedback and
                |   pitch new ideas. We decided that a lottery-style system created an equal playing field for
                |   individual voters while also balancing feasibility.
              p
                | Now, the vibe would be drawn at random from the votes gathered. The majority vote will have
                |   the odds in their favour, but everyone’s vote now has a shot to be chosen.
        section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="web_interface_features")
          h2.heading-underline Web interface features
          .explanation-wrapper
            div
              p
                | I went on to implement the new voting system in our Arduino code and build the web
                |   interface.
              p
                | The web interface’s original plan was to only show the state of the physical devices. This
                |   was
                |   pointless for everyone in the space when the devices already had state indicators. To
                |   incentivize
                |   visiting the website, I used Spotify, Tidal, and Deezer’s APIs to display song details. I
                |   also added
                |   Add to playlist links that allowed users to quickly add the song to their music streaming
                |   playlist.
                |   This gave non-voters a reason to interact with the system.
            .trailer.subheading.website-embed
              h3.heading-underline Website for Serendipity
              iframe(
                title="Serendipity website" 
                src="https://serendipity.maxnielsen.ca" 
                height="315" 
                width="560"
                )
              a.button-small(
                target="_blank" 
                href="https://serendipity.maxnielsen.ca"
                ) Visit website
        section#reflection.wrapper-padding.article-section
          h2.heading-underline Reflection
          p
            | As the project progressed, it became apparent that workloads were unbalanced. I took on too many
            |   tasks as my knowledge of web, interaction, and system design aligned with this course’s content. My
            |   team members also stuck to their strengths in physical prototyping. Next time, I will focus on
            |   developing new skills while acting as a mentor for others taking over my expected job. This way, we
            |   can distribute tasks more evenly and foster better learning outcomes for each team member.
    // Footer
    include includes/footer